"""Q6 — Where do eVTOL designs concentrate, and how have they moved? The text of the thesis layer (see THESIS_CONTRACT.md).

Every number is a {placeholder} resolved from viz.thesis_q6.numbers(ctx); [fig:name] / [tab:name] cite the items of
viz.thesis_q6.ITEMS; [hl]…[/hl] marks the sentence that depends on a flagged item.
"""

METHOD = """- **Objective:** Where eVTOL designs concentrate, between classes and inside them, and how that concentration moved over time.
- **Data and unit:** Human labels of {n_aircraft} unique aircraft, read per four-year priority window; the window from {partial_start} is not read.
- **Procedure:** Fields whose top answer holds under {field_cut} are combined into archetypes (C, C·W·T, C·U) and class configurations.
- **Test:** Discovery curve against random order; Spearman ρ of each class trace on priority year, {trend_min} aircraft or more.
- **Limit:** Shares, never counts; share levels are not comparable between classes, and nothing here tests a dominant design (Q7)."""

RESULTS = [
    dict(sub="A", title="The design space", text="""[hl]Two fields carry most of the variety, the tail type and the propulsor-unit count ([tab:q6_selected_fields]).[/hl] [hl]Their most common answers hold only {tail_top} and {units_top} of the aircraft.[/hl] [hl]The median aircraft carries {units_median} propulsor units.[/hl] [hl]The five bands hold the aircraft almost evenly, and no count is standard ([fig:q6_propulsor_units_per_class]).[/hl]

At C·U, the class with its propulsor-unit band, the recent aircraft sit in a crowded core of {core_n} archetypes ([fig:q6_archetype_core]). The core is led by Lift + Cruise with nine propulsor units or more and Tilt Propulsor with one to three. The core holds {core_share} of the {span_recent} aircraft. Half of the {w3} aircraft sit in the {half_w3} largest archetypes ([fig:q6_archetype_windows]). In the next window the same half sits in {half_w4}. That is a concentration and not a winner, since the largest archetype of that window holds {cu_top_w4} of it.

No new class has appeared in the last {disc_after_last_class} aircraft, yet new combinations of class, wings and tilt still appear faster than chance ([fig:q6_discovery_curve]). At C·W·T the last hundred aircraft brought {cwt_new} new archetypes against {cwt_exp} by chance. The archetypes seen at that grain are {cwt_found} of the {cwt_chao} the Chao1 floor estimates. The classes compete as a closed set while the combinations of wings and tilt are still being explored."""),
    dict(sub="B", title="Between classes", text="""Tilt Propulsor falls from {tp_w1} of the earliest window's aircraft to {tp_w4} in the last complete one ([fig:q6_class_shares_by_window]). Lift + Cruise rises from {lc_w1} to {lc_w4} over the same windows. The two classes meet in {w3}, at {tp_w3} each ([fig:q6_largest_classes_over_time]). With CVT at {cvt_w4} the three hold {three_w4} of the last complete window. The earliest window rests on {w1_n} aircraft against {w4_n} at the recent end, so its shares are coarse. The evtol.news directory shows the same direction, the tilting classes larger in every window and Lift + Cruise rising (Q4). It pools Tilt Propulsor with CVT and Tilt Wing, so the crossover itself has no outside check."""),
    dict(sub="C", title="Inside each class", text="""No class converges on one layout, what changes is which layout leads ([fig:q6_leading_layout_by_class]). In Lift + Cruise the same layout leads in every window, lift propulsor units on booms, at just under half the class ({slc_lead_w4} in the last complete window). Every one of its {slc_poss} possible configurations is in use. CVT keeps about half of its aircraft in its leading layout, but the leader changes. Up to {w3} it is tilting propulsors with the fixed units elsewhere on the airframe, at {cvt_re_w3} of the class in that window. In the last complete window it is tilting propulsors with the fixed units on booms ({cvt_rb_w4}), the boom layout of Lift + Cruise with a tilting set added.

Tilt Propulsor spreads out. The layout with one tilting set falls from {tr_one_w1} of the class to {tr_one_w4}. Tilting sets in two or more places lead the last complete window with {tr_twost_w4} of the class."""),
    dict(sub="D", title="Across classes", text="""Read across its three panels, [fig:q6_leading_layout_by_class] shows the classes moving toward one airframe, a fixed wing carrying many propulsor units on booms. CVT moves its fixed propulsor units onto booms, from {cvt_onb_w1} of its aircraft to {cvt_onb_w4} ([fig:q6_cvt_units_on_booms], [fig:q6_boom_share_by_class]). That share is close to Lift + Cruise, which keeps {slc_onb_w4} of its aircraft on booms and moves on neither booms nor ducts ([fig:q6_ducted_share_by_class]). Tilt Propulsor adds a second tilting set, and its median propulsor units go from {tr_units_w1} to {tr_units_w4} ([fig:q6_class_centres_tilting_units], [fig:q6_tp_units_by_tilting_sets]).

The duct leaves CVT in two steps. First the layout moves onto booms while the aircraft without booms keep their ducts. Then the boom layout sheds its own, from {cvt_duct_booms_w3} to {cvt_duct_booms_w4} ([fig:q6_cvt_ducted_by_boom_layout]).

Of the {traces_moving} traces that move inside a class, only the boom and place traces point to a single driver, distributed propulsion ([tab:q6_driver_verdicts]). The propulsor-unit count is predicted by three drivers at once, and the labelled dataset cannot say which acts. In morphology CVT becomes more like Lift + Cruise, and that likeness defines the family that Q7 tests as the dominant design."""),
]

ANSWER = """The variety of an eVTOL design lies in its propulsion, read down to how many propulsor units it carries and whether any of them tilts. The airframe fields have one leading answer each. The twelve classes are a closed set, with no new class in the last {disc_after_last_class} aircraft. The recent aircraft crowd into a core of {core_n} C·U archetypes, and no archetype holds more than {cu_top_w4} of the last complete window. Between the classes Lift + Cruise overtakes Tilt Propulsor, rising to {lc_w4} of the last complete window while Tilt Propulsor falls to {tp_w4}. Inside each class no layout takes the whole class, what changes is which layout leads. The moves point one way, toward a fixed wing carrying many propulsor units on booms, which brings CVT close to Lift + Cruise and gives Q7 its candidate family."""

